# Testing and verification
- Preserve existing test runner and lint setup; never silently add a new test framework.
- For bugs, write or update a reproducing regression test when practical.
- Prefer unit tests of pure functions/hooks and integration tests of visible user behavior over brittle implementation details.
- Cover boundary conditions, loading/errors, empty results, async cancellation and interactions where relevant.
- When project scripts support it, run `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npx expo lint` and existing test script. If unavailable, report this honestly.
- Do not alter unrelated tests or reduce assertions merely to make checks pass.
